    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "This is a pure mathematical/ML problem (not materials/physics), so DFT/MD skills are inappropriate. I will design a Python script to test the topological rigidity hypothesis: generate synthetic constraints, train small feedforward networks with varying hidden widths (N_c), and measure whether N_c(w) stays constant or grows as constraint count (w) increases. I'll use a lightweight numerical experiment with synthetic data (not heavy simulation) to validate the claim about vanishing first homology in the feasible manifold. If the script runs successfully, I'll analyze N_c(w) trends to determine if the solution space is rigid (constant N_c) or fat (increasing N_c)."
